 "text": "Hey there, how are you doing? Sure, esire means to do something regularly, like walking, and ye is very informal for you. So esire ye means do you walk? That's right. Esta would work too, it' just more formal. That's at your desk for office people, or on the farm for everyone else. It comes from the fact that desks have names on them. It' a bit of a dead language now. That's another one that's falling out of use. It means your clothes for doing the laundry, like washing machines. I' glad I could help. These little phrases still pop up now and then, so it's good to know them.",
